6. PARAMETER EXPLORATION & RESULTS
6.1 Parameter Space Exploration
We systematically explored the parameter space to identify the optimal configuration.

6.1.1 Evolution Strategies Parameters
Parameter	Tested Values	Optimal	Rationale
es_samples	3, 5, 7, 10	5	Balance quality/time
es_sigma	0.02, 0.05, 0.08, 0.12, 0.15	0.08	Strong enough exploration without collapse
es_alpha	0.01, 0.02, 0.03, 0.05	0.03	Stable convergence
Exploration Results:

(samples, sigma, alpha)	Final Novelty	Utility	Stability
(3, 0.05, 0.02)	0.087	0.42	0.91
(5, 0.08, 0.03)	0.151	0.54	0.85
(7, 0.12, 0.05)	0.112	0.31	0.68
Conclusion: (5, 0.08, 0.03) optimizes the exploration-stability tradeoff.

6.1.2 Residual Mixing Parameters
Parameter	Tested	Optimal	Failure Mode
residual_mix_base	0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.5	0.2	0.5→state locking
residual_mix_range	0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4	0.3	Range 0→no adaptation
The Critical Failure:

When residual_mix_base = 0.5 (50% identity mixing), the system exhibited:

text
Residual Locking Failure:
- State updates: 50% previous + 50% new
- Result: Trajectory freezing
- Novelty: collapsed to 0.02
- Utility: maintained artificially (due to inertia)
Mathematical Explanation:

With high residual mixing, the state update approximates:

