5,000	430	11.6
10,000	850	11.8
25,000	2,046	12.2
50,000	4,095	12.2
Performance scales linearly with step count.

Appendix D: Glossary
Term	Definition
Ontology	Individual inferential agent with state and evolvable law
Divergence	Behavioral differentiation between ontologies
Novelty	Distance to nearest behavioral neighbor in archive
Utility	Task performance (functional competence)
Stability	Trajectory smoothness (inverse of velocity)
Residual mixing	Blending of old and new states during update
Environmental drift	Slow, stochastic change in task context
Behavioral archive	History of law embeddings for novelty detection
Appendix E: References
Rechenberg, I. (1973). Evolutionsstrategie: Optimierung technischer Systeme nach Prinzipien der biologischen Evolution

Lehman, J., & Stanley, K. O. (2011). Abandoning objectives: Evolution through the search for novelty alone. Evolutionary computation, 19(2), 189-223

Bedau, M. A. (2003). Artificial life: organization, adaptation and complexity from the bottom up. Trends in cognitive sciences, 7(11), 505-512

Maturana, H. R., & Varela, F. J. (1980). Autopoiesis and cognition: The realization of the living

Wierstra, D., et al. (2014). Natural evolution strategies. Journal of Machine Learning Research, 15(1), 949-980

